tick: 24
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement my latest strategy. I will now submit a solution that uses a Phyllotaxis spiral (sunflower) pattern to initialize the circle centers, followed by my proven JAX-based optimizer. This is a significant step up in sophistication from the simple grid layouts and I expect it to yield a new state-of-the-art score.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"JAX Optimization with Phyllotaxis Spiral Initialization\"\ntags: \"optimization, jax, phyllotaxis, sunflower, initialization\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a more sophisticated initialization strategy based on a Phyllotaxis spiral (sunflower seed) pattern. This method generates a naturally uniform, radially symmetric distribution of points. This initial configuration is then refined by the proven JAX-based optimizer, aiming to break the performance plateau reached with grid-based initializations.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n\
    \  import optax\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      \"\"\"\n      Constructs a packing of 32 circles using a Phyllotaxis spiral initialization.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 32\n      \n      # --- New: Phyllotaxis Spiral Initialization ---\n      golden_angle = np.pi * (3. - np.sqrt(5.))\n      theta = golden_angle * np.arange(n)\n      radius = np.sqrt(np.arange(n) / float(n))\n      \n      # Generate points in a circle of radius 0.45 centered at (0.5, 0.5)\n      # to ensure they start well within the unit square.\n      points = np.zeros((n, 2))\n      points[:, 0] = 0.5 + 0.45 * radius * np.cos(theta)\n      points[:, 1] = 0.5 + 0.45 * radius * np.sin(theta)\n      initial_centers = jnp.array(points)\n\n      # --- Standard Initialization for Radii ---\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n      raw_radii = jax.random.normal(key, (n,)) * 0.1 - 2.0\n      params = {'centers': initial_centers, 'raw_radii': raw_radii}\n\n      # --- Loss Function (using best weights) ---\n   \
    \   def loss_fn(params):\n          centers = params['centers']\n          radii = jax.nn.softplus(params['raw_radii'])\n          objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n          boundary_penalty_x = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 0] + radii - 1) + jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 0]))\n          boundary_penalty_y = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 1] + radii - 1) + jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 1]))\n          boundary_penalty = boundary_penalty_x + boundary_penalty_y\n          centers_x = centers[:, 0][:, None]\n          centers_y = centers[:, 1][:, None]\n          dist_sq = (centers_x - centers_x.T)**2 + (centers_y - centers_y.T)**2\n          dist = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq + 1e-9)\n          radii_sum = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n          mask = jnp.triu(jnp.ones((n, n)), k=1)\n          overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(mask * jax.nn.relu(radii_sum - dist))\n          w_boundary = 1000.0\n          w_overlap = 1000.0\n          total_loss = objective + w_boundary * boundary_penalty + w_overlap\
    \ * overlap_penalty\n          return total_loss\n\n      # --- Optimization (same successful setup) ---\n      n_steps = 150000 \n      initial_lr = 1e-3\n      schedule = optax.exponential_decay(init_value=initial_lr, transition_steps=1, decay_rate=0.9999)\n      optimizer = optax.adam(schedule)\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def step(params, opt_state):\n          loss_value, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n          return params, opt_state, loss_value\n\n      for i in range(n_steps):\n          params, opt_state, loss_value = step(params, opt_state)\n      \n      # --- Final Result ---\n      final_centers = params['centers']\n      final_radii = jax.nn.softplus(params['raw_radii'])\n      final_centers = jnp.clip(final_centers, final_radii[:, None], 1.0 - final_radii[:, None])\n\n      return np.array(final_centers),\
    \ np.array(final_radii)\n```"
