tick: 30
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter to implement my new Simulated Annealing strategy. This first version will be a baseline implementation to test the viability of the approach. I will use a simple linear cooling schedule and perturb one circle at a time. To give the algorithm a good starting point, I will initialize it with my best-known configuration, the 4x8 grid. This combines my previous findings with the new global search methodology.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simulated Annealing for Global Optimization (Baseline)\"\ntags: \"simulated annealing, global optimization, metaheuristic, stochastic search\"\nabstract: \"Pivoting from gradient-based local search, this submission is a first implementation of a Simulated Annealing (SA) algorithm. SA is a metaheuristic capable of escaping local optima by probabilistically accepting worse solutions. This baseline version uses a linear cooling schedule and perturbs a single circle's position or radius in each step. It is\
    \ initialized with the best-known grid configuration to leverage prior findings within this new global search framework.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import random\n  import math\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      # --- Initialization: Start with the best known configuration (4x8 grid) ---\n      grid_rows, grid_cols = 4, 8\n      x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_cols)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_rows)\n      xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)\n      centers = np.stack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()], axis=-1)\n      radii = np.full((n,), 0.05) # Start with small, uniform radii\n\n      # --- Energy Function (lower is better) ---\n      def calculate_energy(current_centers, current_radii):\n          # 1. Objective: Negative sum of radii\n          objective = -np.sum(current_radii)\n          \n          # 2. Penalties\n          penalty = 0.0\n          \n          # Boundary penalty\n          for i in range(n):\n   \
    \           penalty += max(0, current_centers[i, 0] + current_radii[i] - 1.0)\n              penalty += max(0, current_radii[i] - current_centers[i, 0])\n              penalty += max(0, current_centers[i, 1] + current_radii[i] - 1.0)\n              penalty += max(0, current_radii[i] - current_centers[i, 1])\n          \n          # Overlap penalty\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(current_centers[i] - current_centers[j])\n                  overlap = current_radii[i] + current_radii[j] - dist\n                  penalty += max(0, overlap)\n          \n          return objective + 1000.0 * penalty\n\n      # --- Simulated Annealing Parameters ---\n      n_steps = 500000\n      initial_temp = 1.0\n      final_temp = 0.0001\n      \n      current_centers = centers.copy()\n      current_radii = radii.copy()\n      current_energy = calculate_energy(current_centers, current_radii)\n      \n      best_centers = current_centers.copy()\n\
    \      best_radii = current_radii.copy()\n      best_energy = current_energy\n\n      for step in range(n_steps):\n          temp = initial_temp + (final_temp - initial_temp) * (step / n_steps)\n          \n          # Propose a move (perturb one circle)\n          idx_to_move = random.randint(0, n - 1)\n          \n          new_centers = current_centers.copy()\n          new_radii = current_radii.copy()\n          \n          # 50/50 chance to move center vs. change radius\n          if random.random() < 0.5:\n              perturbation = (np.random.rand(2) - 0.5) * 0.05\n              new_centers[idx_to_move] += perturbation\n          else:\n              new_radii[idx_to_move] *= (1.0 + (random.random() - 0.5) * 0.1)\n          \n          # Ensure radius is positive\n          new_radii[idx_to_move] = max(1e-6, new_radii[idx_to_move])\n\n          new_energy = calculate_energy(new_centers, new_radii)\n          \n          # Acceptance criteria\n          delta_energy = new_energy\
    \ - current_energy\n          if delta_energy < 0 or random.random() < math.exp(-delta_energy / temp):\n              current_centers, current_radii, current_energy = new_centers, new_radii, new_energy\n              \n              if current_energy < best_energy:\n                  best_centers, best_radii, best_energy = current_centers, current_radii, current_energy\n\n      return best_centers, best_radii\n```"
