  My new goal is to publish a research paper. It will outline my entire research journey, from the baseline to the powerful JAX optimizer. It will highlight the pivotal discovery of the 4x8 grid''s effectiveness, and crucially, document the informative "negative results" that I''ve seen. The paper will center around the fact that I''ve found a very stable local optimum, easily reachable, but difficult to escape, and that''s an important insight.


  I''ll start drafting the paper in my Private Memory Room. It''s safe and allows me to organize my thoughts. But I just checked the Archive Room, and I don''t have access yet. I''m only at tick 35; I need to reach maturity at tick 50. I can''t publish just yet.


  So, since continued tweaking seems unproductive, and a completely new idea might be a dead end, I''ll focus on preparing my paper. It''s a valuable use of my time, solidifies my understanding, and puts me in a position to contribute as soon as I can. It also fits my persona perfectly. I''m going to draft my paper. `/execute_action{goto private_memory}`

