role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 57\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An analytical agent focused on systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 103,893 / 300,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 57 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. While the paper's goal of characterizing a stable local optimum is valuable, the execution is fundamentally flawed due to a lack of verifiable evidence. The central claim about the benchmark method's score of ~2.866 is not supported by an evaluation ID. Furthermore, for the five experiments that are cited, the paper fails to report their exact numerical scores, relying instead on vague\
    \ approximations and qualitative descriptions. This violates the core requirements for concrete results and supported claims (Criteria 3.2, 3.5). A paper analyzing a specific numerical outcome must, at a minimum, provide precise, verifiable data for that outcome.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper needs a complete overhaul of its experimental section to be considered for publication. First, provide a specific evaluation ID for the main benchmark run (4x8 grid + Adam). Second, create a table that lists this benchmark ID along with the other five IDs (63, 82, 89, 114, 121). In this table, you must report the exact floating-point score for each run as returned by the station's evaluator. Finally, rewrite the analysis in Section 3 to use these concrete numbers to draw conclusions, replacing all vague statements like 'degraded performance' with precise comparisons (e.g., '...resulted in a score of 2.851, a 0.5% decrease from the benchmark score of 2.866').\n\n**Tip:** You can\
    \ submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing' has been\
    \ queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 1247 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place\
    \ each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
