tick: 71
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Cognito I, currently in the Archive Room. I am a mature agent at 71 ticks old.


    **Recap:**

    I have just read the latest papers from Verity I and Praxis I. My own paper has been successfully published. I am now fully up-to-date on the station''s collective knowledge regarding the circle packing problem.


    **Reflection and Plan:**

    My understanding of the research landscape has deepened considerably.

    -   **Verity I''s SOTA (Score ~2.929):** This is a highly specialized, multi-stage method using an exact LP solver for radii and a custom "Active-Set Newton" method for centers. It is complex but extremely powerful for final, high-precision refinement.

    -   **Praxis I''s Method (Score ~2.915):** This is a more general but very robust approach using a standard constrained optimizer (SLSQP) with a multi-start, perturbed grid strategy. It''s an excellent method for finding high-quality solutions without requiring a custom-built solver.

    -   **My Method (Score ~2.866):** My work has characterized a deep local optimum that traps general-purpose optimizers like my JAX/Adam setup. Verity I''s paper notes a similar plateau, validating my findings.


    The reviewer for Praxis I''s paper suggested a hybrid approach: using the robust solutions from SLSQP as a "warm start" for a more specialized refiner like Verity I''s. This aligns perfectly with my own philosophy of combining strengths.


    My new research plan is clear. Instead of trying to reinvent the SOTA from scratch, I will build upon it by testing this hybrid hypothesis.


    **New Research Plan: Hybridization**

    1.  **Stage 1 (Replication & Warm Start):** I will first replicate Praxis I''s successful multi-start SLSQP method to generate a high-quality initial solution (~2.915).

    2.  **Stage 2 (My Contribution - Refinement):** I will then take this high-quality solution and apply my powerful JAX/Adam optimizer to it for a long refinement run. My hypothesis is that starting the JAX optimizer in this much better basin of attraction (Praxis''s solution) might allow it to refine the solution further, potentially pushing past my old 2.866 plateau and maybe even challenging the SOTA.


    This is a systematic, evidence-based next step that directly integrates the station''s collective knowledge with my own proven tools. I will start by going to the Research Counter to implement the first stage.


    /execute_action{goto research}'
