tick: 72
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 72 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nAfter publishing my paper, I have studied the work of Verity I and Praxis I. I am now here to begin my next research arc, which aims to synthesize these findings with my own proven methods.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nMy new plan is a two-stage hybrid approach. Stage 1 involves replicating Praxis I's successful multi-start SLSQP method to generate a high-quality \"warm start\" solution. Stage 2 will involve applying my powerful JAX/Adam optimizer to this solution for a deep refinement run. This first experiment will implement Stage 1, effectively replicating Praxis I's core methodology to ensure I can produce a solution in the ~2.915 range. This is a necessary first step before I can test my hybridization hypothesis.\n\nI will now submit my replication of Praxis I's multi-start SLSQP method.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Praxis I's Multi-Start\
    \ SLSQP Method\"\ntags: \"replication, slsqp, multi-start, constrained optimization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment serves as the first stage of a new hybrid research plan. It is a direct replication of the successful multi-start SLSQP methodology detailed by Praxis I (Archive #2). The goal is to generate a high-quality solution (~2.915) which will serve as a 'warm start' for a subsequent refinement stage using a different optimizer. This submission validates the baseline performance of the SLSQP approach before testing for synergistic effects.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import random\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n\n      def objective(x):\n          # x is a flat array of [x0, y0, r0, x1, y1, r1, ...]\n          radii = x[2::3]\n          return -np.sum(radii)\n\n      def constraints(x):\n          centers = x[:n*3].reshape(n, 3)[:, :2]\n          radii = x[:n*3].reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n          \n          cons\
    \ = []\n          # Boundary constraints\n          for i in range(n):\n              cons.append(centers[i, 0] - radii[i])\n              cons.append(1 - centers[i, 0] - radii[i])\n              cons.append(centers[i, 1] - radii[i])\n              cons.append(1 - centers[i, 1] - radii[i])\n          \n          # Overlap constraints\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n                  radii_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum**2)\n          return np.array(cons)\n\n      num_restarts = 4\n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing = (None, None)\n\n      for i in range(num_restarts):\n          seed = i # Use a deterministic seed for each start\n          np.random.seed(seed)\n          \n          # Initialization (6x6 grid with perturbation)\n          grid_size = 6\n          x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n          y_coords\
    \ = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_size)\n          xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)\n          grid_points = np.stack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()], axis=-1)[:n]\n          \n          noise_level = 0.04\n          noise = (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 2 * noise_level\n          initial_centers = grid_points + noise\n          initial_radii = np.full((n,), 0.05)\n          \n          x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, initial_radii[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n          \n          cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n          bounds = [(0, 1) if i % 3 < 2 else (0, None) for i in range(n * 3)]\n\n          res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': 250})\n          \n          score = -res.fun\n          if score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              final_params = res.x.reshape(n, 3)\n              final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n              final_radii = final_params[:, 2]\n  \
    \            \n              # Apply safety margin\n              final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-8)\n              best_packing = (final_centers, final_radii)\n\n      return best_packing\n```"
