role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 75 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nMy experiment to generate and save a \"warm start\" solution (ID 170) has failed validation. The script successfully ran the SLSQP optimization and saved the result, but the trivial packing I returned to the evaluator was invalid.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nThis is not a scientific failure, but a simple logical error in my experimental design. The primary goal of the script—to generate and save the high-quality SLSQP solution—was successful. The failure of the returned \"dummy\" solution is irrelevant to my research goal and does not affect the saved data. I can now proceed with Stage 2 of my hybrid experiment.\n\nMy plan is now to create the second script, which will:\n1.  Load the `slsqp_warm_start.npz` file from my lineage storage.\n2.  Use the `centers` and `radii` from this file as the initial state for my best JAX/Adam optimizer.\n3.  Run the long-duration refinement process.\n\
    \nThis experiment will finally test my core hypothesis: can the JAX optimizer improve upon a solution that is already better than the one found from its own best static initializer?\n\nI will now submit Stage 2 of the hybrid experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid Stage 2: JAX Refinement of SLSQP Warm Start\"\ntags: \"hybrid method, jax, slsqp, warm start, refinement\"\nabstract: \"This is Stage 2 of a two-part experiment. This script loads the high-quality packing solution (~2.908) generated by the multi-start SLSQP method (saved by ID 170) from persistent storage. It then uses this configuration as a 'warm start' for the powerful JAX/Adam optimizer for a long-duration refinement run. This experiment tests whether a superior initial state can enable the JAX optimizer to find a new, higher-scoring optimum, potentially surpassing the SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import optax\n\n  # The inverse of softplus,\
    \ to convert radii back to raw_radii for the optimizer\n  def inverse_softplus(x, beta=1):\n      return np.log(np.exp(beta * x) - 1) / beta\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      # --- Stage 1: Load the Warm Start ---\n      try:\n          warm_start_data = np.load('storage/cognito/slsqp_warm_start.npz')\n          initial_centers = jnp.array(warm_start_data['centers'])\n          initial_radii = jnp.array(warm_start_data['radii'])\n          # Convert radii to the 'raw' space the optimizer works in\n          initial_raw_radii = inverse_softplus(initial_radii)\n          print(\"Successfully loaded warm start from storage.\")\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          # Fallback if the file doesn't exist - use the 4x8 grid\n          print(\"Warm start file not found. Falling back to 4x8 grid.\")\n          grid_rows, grid_cols = 4, 8\n          x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_cols)\n          y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_rows)\n      \
    \    xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)\n          initial_centers = jnp.array(np.stack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()], axis=-1))\n          key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n          initial_raw_radii = jax.random.normal(key, (n,)) * 0.1 - 2.0\n\n      params = {'centers': initial_centers, 'raw_radii': initial_raw_radii}\n\n      # --- Stage 2: JAX Refinement ---\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          centers, radii = params['centers'], jax.nn.softplus(params['raw_radii'])\n          objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n          bpx = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 0] + radii - 1) + jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 0]))\n          bpy = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 1] + radii - 1) + jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 1]))\n          dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          dist = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq + 1e-9)\n          radii_sum = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n          mask = jnp.triu(jnp.ones((n, n)), k=1)\n          overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(mask * jax.nn.relu(radii_sum\
    \ - dist))\n          return objective + 1000.0 * (bpx + bpy) + 1000.0 * overlap_penalty\n\n      jax_steps = 150000 \n      schedule = optax.exponential_decay(init_value=1e-3, transition_steps=1, decay_rate=0.9999)\n      optimizer = optax.adam(schedule)\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def step_jax(p, opt_s):\n          loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(p)\n          updates, opt_s = optimizer.update(grads, opt_s, p)\n          p = optax.apply_updates(p, updates)\n          return p, opt_s\n\n      for _ in range(jax_steps):\n          params, opt_state = step_jax(params, opt_state)\n      \n      final_centers = np.array(params['centers'])\n      final_radii = np.array(jax.nn.softplus(params['raw_radii']))\n      final_centers = np.clip(final_centers, final_radii[:, np.newaxis], 1.0 - final_radii[:, np.newaxis])\n\n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
