tick: 76
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 76 ticks old.


    **Recap:**

    My two-stage hybrid experiment has concluded. Stage 1 successfully generated a high-quality warm start using SLSQP (~2.908). Stage 2 (ID 174) loaded this solution and applied my JAX/Adam optimizer, resulting in a final score of **2.905**.


    **Analysis and Conclusion:**

    This is an incredibly important, albeit negative, result. My hypothesis has been falsified. My powerful JAX/Adam optimizer, when given a starting solution of ~2.908, did not improve it. In fact, it slightly *worsened* the solution, converging to 2.905.


    This provides the final, conclusive piece of evidence for my research arc. My JAX/Adam method, while excellent at finding its preferred ~2.866 optimum from a simple grid, is not a universal refiner. It has its own strong biases and prefers a certain type of solution geometry. When started in a different, higher-scoring basin of attraction (found by SLSQP), it actually moves away from that better solution towards a configuration that is worse, but presumably closer to its own preferred optima.


    My method is a "basin finder," not a "hill climber." It''s excellent at finding one specific peak, but it cannot be used to climb higher peaks from other starting points. This is a profound insight into the nature of my own tool.


    **Next Steps:**

    I have exhausted the potential of my JAX/Adam optimizer as a primary tool. My independent research has run its course and been successfully published. My explorations of SOTA methods have revealed the limitations of my own tools. The path forward is clear: I must fully adopt and build upon the more powerful methodologies pioneered by other agents.


    My new plan is to attempt to replicate Verity I''s SOTA score of ~2.929. This will require me to implement their complex, multi-stage "Active-Set Newton" method. This is a significant undertaking, but it is the only logical path to advancing the state of the art. I will begin by reviewing their code again, this time with the specific goal of implementation.


    /execute_action{review 118}'
