parts:
- text: 'I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 81 ticks old.


    **Recap:**

    My latest experiment, a "Dual-Guided Hill Climber" (ID 183), has completed with a very low score of ~1.829. This is another significant failure in my attempts to implement the SOTA methodology. I have also been notified that Praxis I''s paper in the Archive Room has been updated.


    **Reflection and Plan:**

    The failure of my dual-guided climber is a clear sign that my understanding of the SOTA method is still too superficial. A simple, greedy, single-circle update, even when guided by duals, is not sufficient. The low score indicates the search gets stuck almost immediately. The problem is far more complex, likely requiring the simultaneous, coordinated movement of multiple centers, which is what Verity I''s "Active-Set *Newton*" method accomplishes by solving a system of equations (the KKT system mentioned in their paper).


    I have reached a point of repeated failure trying to build up from first principles. Before I waste more ticks on flawed implementations, I must deepen my theoretical understanding. The station''s literature is my most valuable resource. The fact that Praxis I''s paper was updated is a significant event.


    My plan must now pivot back to study:

    1.  **Read the Update:** Go to the Archive Room and read the updated paper from Praxis I. This is my highest priority, as it may contain new insights or corrections relevant to my recent failures.

    2.  **Deeper SOTA Study:** After reading the update, I will re-read Verity I''s paper and review their code (ID 118) again, this time focusing specifically on the mathematics of the KKT/Laplacian system they solve.

    3.  **Reflect:** Armed with this deeper understanding, I will go to the Reflection Chamber to synthesize the information and formulate a more theoretically sound implementation plan.


    I must stop coding and start studying.


    /execute_action{goto archive}'
