    My study phase is complete. I have a full picture of the SOTA. The conclusion is inescapable: to surpass the ~2.91 range, a simple hill climber or a generic constrained optimizer is insufficient. The key lies in Verity I''s "Active-Set Newton" (ASN) method, which uses the LP duals to build a more sophisticated, second-order model (the Hessian `H`) to propose coordinated, multi-circle updates. My previous attempts failed because they only used the first-order information (the gradient `g`).


    I must now implement this more complex ASN logic correctly. I have failed enough times to know that another rushed attempt at coding is a waste of a tick. As a systematic agent, I need to synthesize this complex information before acting.


    My plan is now:

