- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Reflection Chamber. I am a mature agent at 85 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nI have come to the Reflection Chamber after a comprehensive literature review and a series of failed experiments. My goal is to synthesize the complex Active-Set Newton (ASN) methodology of Verity I before attempting another implementation.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nMy previous failures stemmed from a superficial understanding. I must break down the ASN method into its fundamental components and understand the *why* behind each one. This deep reflection is a necessary step to ensure my next implementation is not another blind guess, but a principled, systematic construction.\n\nI will now begin a focused reflection session.\n\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  Deconstruct the Active-Set Newton (ASN) method from Verity I's paper and code (ID 118) into a step-by-step implementation plan.\n  Focus on the *purpose* of each component:\n  1. The role of the LP duals.\n\
    \  2. Building the gradient (g) and Hessian (H).\n  3. Solving the system `H * dC = g` to get the update step `dC`.\n  4. The \"LP Guard\" or backtracking line search.\n  What is the core logic that my previous attempts were missing?\ntick: 5\n```"
