tick: 87
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 87 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nI have arrived from the Reflection Chamber with a detailed and robust implementation plan (\"ASN v1.1\") for a simplified Active-Set Newton method. This plan is the synthesis of my learnings from studying the SOTA and analyzing my own experimental failures.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nThe time for study and reflection is over. My next action is to execute the plan I have carefully constructed. I will now implement the ASN v1.1 blueprint. This code will be my most sophisticated attempt to date, incorporating a second-order optimization model, dual smoothing, Hessian damping, and an LP-guarded line search. I am confident that this principled approach has a much higher chance of success than my previous naive attempts.\n\nI will now submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Principled ASN v1.1 Implementation with LP Guard\"\ntags: \"active-set newton,\
    \ asn, second-order, dual-guided, lp-guard\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a robust, first-principles implementation of a simplified Active-Set Newton (ASN) method, based on the blueprint developed in my recent reflection. It uses LP duals to build a local second-order quadratic model (Gradient and Hessian) of the landscape. It then solves for the optimal multi-circle Newton step and uses a backtracking line search, guarded by an exact LP solve at each step, to ensure progress. The method includes dual smoothing and Hessian damping for stability. This is a systematic attempt to correctly implement the core logic of the SOTA methodology.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import time\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      I_triu, J_triu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n\n      def solve_lp(centers: np.ndarray):\n          c_obj = -np.ones(n)\n          D = np.linalg.norm(centers[I_triu] - centers[J_triu], axis=1)\n          m_pairs\
    \ = len(I_triu)\n          A_pairs = np.zeros((m_pairs, n)); A_pairs[np.arange(m_pairs), I_triu] = 1; A_pairs[np.arange(m_pairs), J_triu] = 1\n          b_pairs = D\n          A_bounds = np.zeros((n * 4, n)); b_bounds = np.zeros(n * 4)\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_bounds[i*4+0, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+0] = centers[i, 0]\n              A_bounds[i*4+1, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n              A_bounds[i*4+2, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+2] = centers[i, 1]\n              A_bounds[i*4+3, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n          A_ub = np.vstack([A_pairs, A_bounds]); b_ub = np.concatenate([b_pairs, b_bounds])\n          res = linprog(c_obj, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n          if not res.success or res.x is None: return None, -1.0, None\n          duals = res.ineqlin.marginals[:m_pairs] if hasattr(res, 'ineqlin') and res.ineqlin.marginals is not None else np.zeros(m_pairs)\n          return res.x, -res.fun, np.maximum(0,\
    \ duals)\n\n      # --- ASN v1.1 Blueprint ---\n      MAIN_LOOP_STEPS = 30\n      TIME_BUDGET_SECONDS = 1000\n      LINE_SEARCH_ALPHAS = [1.0, 0.7, 0.4, 0.2]\n      DAMPING_MU = 1e-3\n      DUAL_SMOOTHING_BETA = 0.6\n      IMPROVEMENT_EPSILON = 1e-9\n\n      # 1. Initialization\n      centers = np.array(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 8), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 4))).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n      _, current_score, initial_duals = solve_lp(centers)\n      if initial_duals is None: return centers, np.full(n, 0.01)\n      smoothed_duals = initial_duals\n      start_time = time.time()\n\n      # 2. Main Loop\n      for _ in range(MAIN_LOOP_STEPS):\n          if time.time() - start_time > TIME_BUDGET_SECONDS: break\n\n          # Build Model\n          grad = np.zeros_like(centers)\n          hessian = np.zeros((n, 2, 2))\n          active_mask = smoothed_duals > 1e-9\n          active_duals = smoothed_duals[active_mask]\n          I_act, J_act = I_triu[active_mask], J_triu[active_mask]\n     \
    \     \n          V = centers[I_act] - centers[J_act]\n          d = np.linalg.norm(V, axis=1, keepdims=True); d = np.maximum(d, 1e-9)\n          U = V / d\n          \n          np.add.at(grad, I_act, active_duals[:, np.newaxis] * U)\n          np.add.at(grad, J_act, -active_duals[:, np.newaxis] * U)\n          \n          I2 = np.eye(2)\n          uuT = U[:, :, np.newaxis] * U[:, np.newaxis, :]\n          M_orth = (active_duals[:, np.newaxis, np.newaxis] / d[:,:,np.newaxis]) * (I2 - uuT)\n          np.add.at(hessian, I_act, M_orth)\n          np.add.at(hessian, J_act, M_orth)\n          \n          hessian += DAMPING_MU * np.eye(2)[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          for i in range(n):\n              if np.linalg.det(hessian[i]) < 1e-12: hessian[i] += DAMPING_MU * np.eye(2)\n\n          # Solve for dC\n          try:\n              dC = np.linalg.solve(hessian, grad)\n          except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n              dC = grad # Fallback to simple gradient if solve fails\n\n        \
    \  # Guarded Update\n          move_accepted = False\n          for alpha in LINE_SEARCH_ALPHAS:\n              C_proposed = np.clip(centers + alpha * dC, 0.01, 0.99)\n              _, score_prop, duals_prop = solve_lp(C_proposed)\n              if score_prop > current_score + IMPROVEMENT_EPSILON:\n                  centers = C_proposed\n                  current_score = score_prop\n                  smoothed_duals = DUAL_SMOOTHING_BETA * smoothed_duals + (1 - DUAL_SMOOTHING_BETA) * duals_prop\n                  move_accepted = True\n                  break\n          if not move_accepted: break\n\n      # 3. Finalization\n      final_radii, _, _ = solve_lp(centers)\n      if final_radii is None: final_radii = np.full(n, 0.01)\n      return centers, final_radii * 0.99999\n```"
