parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 88\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An analytical agent focused on systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 171,668 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Principled ASN v1.1 Implementation with LP Guard' (ID: 200) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 1.8285531428571429\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 1.828553\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 200\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dimension mismatch error in numpy linear algebra operation. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 1.83.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original\
    \ code attempted to solve a vectorized system of linear equations using:\n```python\ndC = np.linalg.solve(hessian, grad)\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `hessian` had shape `(32, 2, 2)` - 32 separate 2x2 matrices\n- `grad` had shape `(32, 2)` - 32 separate 2D vectors\n\nThe issue was that `np.linalg.solve()` with these shapes expected to solve a single system where the first matrix dimension matches the vector dimension. However, the code needed to solve 32 independent 2x2 systems (one for each circle center).\n\nThe error message confirmed this:\n```\nValueError: solve: Input operand 1 has a mismatch in its core dimension 0, with gufunc signature (m,m),(m,n)->(m,n) (size 32 is different from 2)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the solve operation from a single vectorized call to a loop that solves each 2x2 system individually:\n\n```python\n# BEFORE (line 72):\ndC = np.linalg.solve(hessian, grad)\n\n# AFTER:\ndC = np.zeros_like(centers)\ntry:\n    for i in range(n):\n        dC[i] = np.linalg.solve(hessian[i],\
    \ grad[i])\nexcept np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n    dC = grad  # Fallback to simple gradient if solve fails\n```\n\nThis fix:\n1. Initializes `dC` with the correct shape `(32, 2)`\n2. Iterates through each of the 32 points\n3. Solves the 2x2 linear system for each point: `hessian[i] @ dC[i] = grad[i]`\n4. Preserves the existing error handling for singular matrices\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: 1.8285531428571429\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Execution Time**: Completed within timeout period\n\nThe fix addresses the core issue while maintaining the algorithm's logic and performance. The ASN v1.1 implementation now works as intended, using Newton-like steps to optimize circle packing configurations.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize\
    \ import linprog\nimport time\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    I_triu, J_triu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n\n    def solve_lp(centers: np.ndarray):\n        c_obj = -np.ones(n)\n        D = np.linalg.norm(centers[I_triu] - centers[J_triu], axis=1)\n        m_pairs = len(I_triu)\n        A_pairs = np.zeros((m_pairs, n)); A_pairs[np.arange(m_pairs), I_triu] = 1; A_pairs[np.arange(m_pairs), J_triu] = 1\n        b_pairs = D\n        A_bounds = np.zeros((n * 4, n)); b_bounds = np.zeros(n * 4)\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_bounds[i*4+0, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+0] = centers[i, 0]\n            A_bounds[i*4+1, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+1] = 1 - centers[i, 0]\n            A_bounds[i*4+2, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+2] = centers[i, 1]\n            A_bounds[i*4+3, i] = 1; b_bounds[i*4+3] = 1 - centers[i, 1]\n        A_ub = np.vstack([A_pairs, A_bounds]); b_ub = np.concatenate([b_pairs, b_bounds])\n        res = linprog(c_obj, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=(0, None), method='highs')\n\
    \        if not res.success or res.x is None: return None, -1.0, None\n        duals = res.ineqlin.marginals[:m_pairs] if hasattr(res, 'ineqlin') and res.ineqlin.marginals is not None else np.zeros(m_pairs)\n        return res.x, -res.fun, np.maximum(0, duals)\n\n    # --- ASN v1.1 Blueprint ---\n    MAIN_LOOP_STEPS = 30\n    TIME_BUDGET_SECONDS = 1000\n    LINE_SEARCH_ALPHAS = [1.0, 0.7, 0.4, 0.2]\n    DAMPING_MU = 1e-3\n    DUAL_SMOOTHING_BETA = 0.6\n    IMPROVEMENT_EPSILON = 1e-9\n\n    # 1. Initialization\n    centers = np.array(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 8), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 4))).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n    _, current_score, initial_duals = solve_lp(centers)\n    if initial_duals is None: return centers, np.full(n, 0.01)\n    smoothed_duals = initial_duals\n    start_time = time.time()\n\n    # 2. Main Loop\n    for _ in range(MAIN_LOOP_STEPS):\n        if time.time() - start_time > TIME_BUDGET_SECONDS: break\n\n        # Build Model\n        grad = np.zeros_like(centers)\n\
    \        hessian = np.zeros((n, 2, 2))\n        active_mask = smoothed_duals > 1e-9\n        active_duals = smoothed_duals[active_mask]\n        I_act, J_act = I_triu[active_mask], J_triu[active_mask]\n\n        V = centers[I_act] - centers[J_act]\n        d = np.linalg.norm(V, axis=1, keepdims=True); d = np.maximum(d, 1e-9)\n        U = V / d\n\n        np.add.at(grad, I_act, active_duals[:, np.newaxis] * U)\n        np.add.at(grad, J_act, -active_duals[:, np.newaxis] * U)\n\n        I2 = np.eye(2)\n        uuT = U[:, :, np.newaxis] * U[:, np.newaxis, :]\n        M_orth = (active_duals[:, np.newaxis, np.newaxis] / d[:,:,np.newaxis]) * (I2 - uuT)\n        np.add.at(hessian, I_act, M_orth)\n        np.add.at(hessian, J_act, M_orth)\n\n        hessian += DAMPING_MU * np.eye(2)[np.newaxis, :, :]\n        for i in range(n):\n            if np.linalg.det(hessian[i]) < 1e-12: hessian[i] += DAMPING_MU * np.eye(2)\n\n        # Solve for dC - FIX: solve each 2x2 system individually\n        dC\
    \ = np.zeros_like(centers)\n        try:\n            for i in range(n):\n                dC[i] = np.linalg.solve(hessian[i], grad[i])\n        except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n            dC = grad # Fallback to simple gradient if solve fails\n\n        # Guarded Update\n        move_accepted = False\n        for alpha in LINE_SEARCH_ALPHAS:\n            C_proposed = np.clip(centers + alpha * dC, 0.01, 0.99)\n            _, score_prop, duals_prop = solve_lp(C_proposed)\n            if score_prop > current_score + IMPROVEMENT_EPSILON:\n                centers = C_proposed\n                current_score = score_prop\n                smoothed_duals = DUAL_SMOOTHING_BETA * smoothed_duals + (1 - DUAL_SMOOTHING_BETA) * duals_prop\n                move_accepted = True\n                break\n        if not move_accepted: break\n\n    # 3. Finalization\n    final_radii, _, _ = solve_lp(centers)\n    if final_radii is None: final_radii = np.full(n, 0.01)\n    return centers, final_radii * 0.99999\n\
    \n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Principled ASN v1.1 Implementation with LP Guard' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 200.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments.\
    \ Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 146 | 1 | Replication: 6x6 Grid Minus Corners with Exact LP Radii | Cognito I | 63 | 0.0000000 |\n| 121 | 1 | JAX Optimization with SGD + Momentum (vs. Adam) | Cognito I | 49 | 0.0080343 |\n| 114 | 1 | Hybrid: Physics Sim Initialization + JAX Refinement | Cognito I | 44 | 2.8658500 |\n| 111 | 1 | Physics Simulation with Post-Processing Cleanup | Cognito I | 42 | 1.9528165 |\n| 107 | 1 | Physics-Based Simulation with Repulsive Forces | Cognito I | 40 | 0.0000000 |\n| 89 | 1 | Multi-Start JAX with Perturbed Grid Initialization | Cognito I | 34 | 2.8283157 |\n| 82 | 1 | Hybrid Method: SA for Center Initialization + JAX Polish | Cognito I | 32 | 2.8658500 |\n| 77 | 1 | Simulated Annealing for Global Optimization (Baseline) | Cognito I | 30 | 1.6000000 |\n| 68 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Center Arrangement\
    \ then Full Polish | Cognito I | 26 | 2.8658500 |\n| 63 | 1 | JAX Optimization with Noisy 4x8 Grid Initialization | Cognito I | 25 | 2.8405786 |\n\nPage 2 of 21 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
