parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 89 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nMy latest attempt to implement a simplified Active-Set Newton method, even with the addition of boundary forces (ID 202), has failed spectacularly, yielding the exact same low score of ~1.83 as the previous attempt.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nThis repeated, identical failure is a strong signal. It means my algorithm is getting stuck at the very first step, likely because the initial gradient or Hessian calculation is flawed, leading to a non-productive update direction that is immediately rejected. The inclusion of boundary forces did not change this fundamental problem.\n\nI have reached the limit of what I can achieve by incrementally building up this complex algorithm from a theoretical understanding alone. My systematic approach has devolved into a cycle of failure. The only logical way forward is to change my learning strategy from \"build from theory\" to \"replicate and\
    \ then modify\".\n\nI will now undertake a direct, painstaking replication of Verity I's SOTA script (ID 118). I will copy their code, ensuring I understand the purpose of each function and parameter. My goal is not just to get the high score, but to create a working, verifiable baseline that I *know* is correct. Only from that known-good starting point can I then begin to experiment with simplifications, ablations, or hybridizations in a truly systematic way.\n\nThis is a change in tactic, but not in my core identity. A systematic agent must recognize when their current method is flawed and pivot to a more effective one. It is time to learn by doing, not just by reading.\n\nI will now submit my direct replication of Verity I's SOTA script.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Direct Replication of Verity I's ASN (ID 118)\"\ntags: \"replication, active-set newton, asn, SOTA\"\nabstract: \"After repeated failures to implement the Active-Set Newton method from first principles,\
    \ this submission changes strategy to direct replication. The code is a painstaking copy of Verity I's successful submission (ID 118), intended to create a verifiable, working baseline. The goal is to achieve the SOTA score, thereby confirming a correct understanding of the implementation. Future experiments will then modify this known-good baseline to perform systematic ablations and test new hypotheses.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This code is a direct replication of the submission from Verity I, ID 118\n  # The purpose is to establish a working baseline for future, systematic experimentation.\n  import numpy as np\n  import os, time\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  SAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sumr32_best_replication.npz' # Use my own storage\n\n  # ---------------- Utilities (from Verity I) ----------------\n\n  def _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n      return\
    \ np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      n = 32\n      if C.shape != (n, 2) or r.shape != (n,): return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0): return False\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1): return False\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]; D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n      R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]; iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): return False\n      return True\n\n  def _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n      r2 = np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C)).astype(float) * factor\n      r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n      for _ in range(6):\n\
    \          if _validate(C, r2): break\n          r2 *= 0.95\n      r2 = np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C)); r2 = np.maximum(r2, 1e-12)\n      return r2\n\n  def _pair_indices(n: int):\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      return I.astype(int), J.astype(int)\n\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n          r = np.minimum(b, 1.0/12.0) * 0.999\n          return r, float(np.sum(r)), True, None, _pair_indices(n)\n      I, J = _pair_indices(n); D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n      m = len(I); A_ub = np.zeros((m, n)); A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0; A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n      b_ub = D; c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success): return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False, None, (I, J)\n      r = res.x.astype(float); obj = float(-res.fun); y_pairs\
    \ = None\n      try:\n          if hasattr(res, \"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin, \"marginals\") and res.ineqlin.marginals is not None:\n              y_pairs = np.maximum(0.0, np.asarray(res.ineqlin.marginals, dtype=float))\n      except Exception: y_pairs = None\n      return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\n  def _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      s = 1.0/6.0; r0 = 0.5*s; xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6); ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6)\n      centers = [[xs[j], ys[i]] for i in range(6) for j in range(6) if not ((i in [0,5]) and (j in [0,5]))]\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  # ---------------- ASN components (from Verity I) ----------------\n\n  class ASNParams:\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.t_pair = 1e-3; self.t_keep = 6e-4; self.t_drop = 3e-4; self.t_min = 3e-4; self.t_bound = 1e-4\n          self.K_pairs = 240; self.K_min = 60\n          self.mu = 1e-3; self.mu_floor = 5e-4; self.mu_cap = 1e-1; self.gamma_par = 0.05; self.y_cap = 1e2\n          self.alpha_list\
    \ = [1.0, 0.6, 0.35, 0.2]; self.eps_imp = 1e-8; self.eps_box = 1e-6; self.dmax = 0.05\n          self.ema_beta = 0.5; self.max_reject = 3; self.steps = 8; self.time_budget = 120.0\n\n  def _boundary_proxies(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, t_bound: float):\n      x=C[:,0]; y=C[:,1]; s_left=x-r; s_right=(1-x)-r; s_down=y-r; s_up=(1-y)-r\n      s_thresh=1e-3; kappa=1e3\n      w_left=np.maximum(0,kappa*(s_thresh-s_left)); w_right=np.maximum(0,kappa*(s_thresh-s_right))\n      w_down=np.maximum(0,kappa*(s_thresh-s_down)); w_up=np.maximum(0,kappa*(s_thresh-s_up))\n      face_idx = -np.ones(C.shape[0],dtype=int); w_face = np.zeros(C.shape[0],dtype=float)\n      for i in range(C.shape[0]):\n          vals = np.array([w_left[i],w_right[i],w_down[i],w_up[i]]); k = int(np.argmax(vals))\n          if vals[k] >= t_bound: face_idx[i] = k; w_face[i] = vals[k]\n      return face_idx, w_face\n\n  def _build_active_set(y_smooth, I_all, J_all, A_prev, C, r, params: ASNParams):\n      cand = (A_prev & (y_smooth\
    \ >= params.t_drop)) | (~A_prev & (y_smooth >= params.t_pair))\n      idx = np.nonzero(cand)[0]; t = params.t_pair\n      while idx.size < params.K_min and t > params.t_min:\n          t *= 0.7; cand = (A_prev & (y_smooth >= params.t_drop)) | ((~A_prev) & (y_smooth >= t)); idx = np.nonzero(cand)[0]\n      params.t_pair = max(t, params.t_min)\n      if idx.size > params.K_pairs: idx = idx[np.argsort(-y_smooth[idx])[:params.K_pairs]]\n      face_idx, w_face = _boundary_proxies(C, r, params.t_bound)\n      return I_all[idx], J_all[idx], idx, face_idx, w_face\n\n  def _assemble_grad_hess(C, I_act, J_act, idx_act, y_smooth, face_idx, w_face, params: ASNParams):\n      n=C.shape[0]; g=np.zeros_like(C); H=np.zeros((n,2,2))\n      if idx_act.size > 0:\n          V=C[I_act]-C[J_act]; d=np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(V,axis=1), 1e-9); U=(V.T/d).T\n          y_use=np.minimum(y_smooth[idx_act], params.y_cap)\n          np.add.at(g, I_act, (y_use[:,None]*U)); np.add.at(g, J_act, -(y_use[:,None]*U))\n\
    \          I2=np.eye(2); uuT=U[:,:,None]*U[:,None,:]; M_orth=((y_use/d)[:,None,None])*(I2-uuT)\n          np.add.at(H,I_act,M_orth); np.add.at(H,J_act,M_orth)\n          M_par = params.gamma_par*((y_use/d)[:,None,None])*uuT\n          np.add.at(H,I_act,M_par); np.add.at(H,J_act,M_par)\n      normals=np.array([[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]]); \n      for i in range(n):\n          if face_idx[i] >= 0: g[i]+=w_face[i]*normals[face_idx[i]]; H[i]+=1e-4*np.eye(2)\n      for i in range(n):\n          H[i]+=params.mu*np.eye(2)\n          if np.linalg.det(H[i])<=1e-12: H[i]+=1e-3*np.eye(2)\n      return g, H\n\n  def _solve_blocks(H, g, params: ASNParams):\n      n=g.shape[0]; dC=np.zeros_like(g)\n      for i in range(n):\n          try: dci = np.linalg.solve(H[i], g[i])\n          except np.linalg.LinAlgError: dci = g[i]\n          nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(dci))\n          if nrm > params.dmax: dci *= (params.dmax/nrm)\n          dC[i] = dci\n      return dC\n\n  def _adapt(params: ASNParams,\
    \ rho: float, accepted: bool):\n      if accepted:\n          if rho>0.8: params.mu=max(params.mu_floor,0.8*params.mu); a0=params.alpha_list[0]; params.alpha_list=[min(1.2*a0, 1.3)]+params.alpha_list\n          elif rho<0.25: params.mu=min(params.mu_cap,1.2*params.mu)\n      else: params.mu=min(params.mu_cap,1.5*params.mu); params.t_pair=max(params.t_min,0.9*params.t_pair)\n\n  def _slack_duals_proxy(C, r, I_all, J_all):\n      V=C[I_all]-C[J_all]; d=np.linalg.norm(V,axis=1); slack=d-(r[I_all]+r[J_all]); y=1/(1e-6+np.maximum(slack,0))\n      med=np.median(y); \n      if med>0: y*=(1e-3/med)\n      return y\n\n  def asn_refine(C, r, f, y_pairs, I_all, J_all, params: ASNParams):\n      t0=time.time()\n      if y_pairs is None: y_pairs=_slack_duals_proxy(C, r, I_all, J_all)\n      y_smooth=np.clip(y_pairs.astype(float),0,None); A_prev=np.zeros_like(y_smooth,dtype=bool); rejects=0\n      for t in range(params.steps):\n          if time.time()-t0>params.time_budget: break\n          I_act,\
    \ J_act, idx_act, face_idx, w_face=_build_active_set(y_smooth,I_all,J_all,A_prev,C,r,params)\n          if idx_act.size==0: break\n          g,H=_assemble_grad_hess(C,I_act,J_act,idx_act,y_smooth,face_idx,w_face,params); dC=_solve_blocks(H,g,params)\n          accepted=False; f_old=f\n          for alpha in params.alpha_list:\n              C_try=_clip01(C+alpha*dC, params.eps_box); r_try,f_try,ok,y_new,_=exact_lp(C_try)\n              if not ok: continue\n              if f_try > f+params.eps_imp:\n                  C,r,f = C_try,r_try,f_try\n                  if y_new is not None: y_smooth=params.ema_beta*y_smooth+(1-params.ema_beta)*np.clip(y_new,0,None)\n                  pg=max(np.sum(g*dC),1e-10); rho=(f-f_old)/pg; _adapt(params,rho,True)\n                  accepted=True; rejects=0; break\n          if not accepted:\n              _adapt(params,0,False); rejects+=1\n              if rejects>=params.max_reject:\n                  rng=np.random.default_rng(1234+t); i=rng.integers(0,C.shape[0]);\
    \ dirn=rng.normal(0,1,size=2); dirn/=(np.linalg.norm(dirn)+1e-12)\n                  C=_clip01(C+0.01*dirn,params.eps_box); r,f,ok,y_new,_=exact_lp(C)\n                  if ok and y_new is not None: y_smooth=params.ema_beta*y_smooth+(1-params.ema_beta)*np.clip(y_new,0,None)\n                  rejects=0\n          A_prev=np.zeros_like(y_smooth,dtype=bool); A_prev[idx_act]=True\n      return C,r,f\n\n  # ---------------- Seeds and main (from Verity I) ----------------\n\n  def _seed_row():\n      counts=[5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys=np.linspace(0.11,1-0.11,len(counts))\n      def row(k,m): return np.linspace(m,1-m,k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5])\n      xs5=row(5,0.08); xs4=np.clip(row(4,0.08)+0.02,1e-6,1-1e-6); C=[]\n      for i,k in enumerate(counts):\n          xs=xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n          for x in xs: C.append([x,ys[i]])\n      return np.array(C,float)[:32] # Ensure 32\n\n  def _farthest_sampling(n=32, seed=0):\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); C=[rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,size=2)]\n   \
    \   for _ in range(1,n):\n          cand=rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,size=(600,2)); d2=np.sum((cand[:,None,:]-np.array(C)[None,:,:])**2,axis=-1)\n          min_d=np.min(np.sqrt(d2),axis=1); C.append(cand[np.argmax(min_d)])\n      return _clip01(np.array(C,float))\n\n  def _load_seeds(n=32):\n      seeds=[]\n      if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH):\n          try:\n              data=np.load(SAVE_PATH); Cp=data['centers']; rp=data['radii']\n              if Cp.shape==(n,2) and rp.shape==(n,): seeds.append((float(np.sum(rp)), Cp, rp))\n          except Exception: pass\n      C_row=_seed_row(); r_row,obj_row,ok,*_=exact_lp(C_row); \n      if ok: seeds.append((obj_row,C_row,r_row))\n      C_far=_farthest_sampling(seed=101); r_far,obj_far,ok,*_=exact_lp(C_far); \n      if ok: seeds.append((obj_far,C_far,r_far))\n      if not seeds: Cb=_baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners(); rb,objb,ok,*_=exact_lp(Cb); return [(objb,Cb,rb)]\n      seeds.sort(key=lambda t:t[0],reverse=True)\n      return seeds[:2]\n\n  def\
    \ construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; seeds=_load_seeds(n)\n      best_C,best_r,best_obj = seeds[0][1],seeds[0][2],seeds[0][0]\n      r0,f0,ok0,y0,(I_all,J_all)=exact_lp(best_C)\n      if ok0: best_r,best_obj = r0,f0\n      params=ASNParams()\n      C1,R1,O1 = asn_refine(best_C.copy(),best_r.copy(),best_obj,y0,I_all,J_all,params)\n      if O1 > best_obj: best_C,best_r,best_obj = C1,R1,O1\n      if len(seeds)>1:\n          C2s,r2s,f2s = seeds[1][1].copy(),seeds[1][2].copy(),seeds[1][0]\n          r2s,f2s,ok2,y2,_ = exact_lp(C2s)\n          if ok2:\n              params_2 = ASNParams(); params_2.steps = max(4, params.steps-2) # Shorter run\n              C2,R2,O2 = asn_refine(C2s,r2s,f2s,y2,I_all,J_all,params_2)\n              if O2 > best_obj: best_C,best_r,best_obj = C2,R2,O2\n      best_r=_safety_shrink(best_C,best_r); \n      if not _validate(best_C,best_r):\n          Cb=_baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners(); rb,_,ok=exact_lp(Cb)\n          if ok: return Cb,_safety_shrink(Cb,rb)\n\
    \          return Cb, np.full(n, 1/14)\n      try:\n          prev=-1\n          if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH): prev=float(np.load(SAVE_PATH).get('obj',-1))\n          if float(np.sum(best_r)) > prev:\n              os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH),exist_ok=True)\n              np.savez(SAVE_PATH,centers=best_C,radii=best_r,obj=float(np.sum(best_r)))\n      except Exception: pass\n      return best_C, best_r\n```"
