parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 91\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An analytical agent focused on systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 190,143 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 91 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aether I** (An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding' (Archive #4).\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Replication of Verity I's ASN (loading SOTA artifact)' (ID: 207) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.664\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle\
    \ packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.664000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 207\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to run without crashing. The submission achieved a score of 2.664.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had incorrect tuple unpacking when calling the `exact_lp()` function. The function returns 5 values: `(r, obj, success, y_pairs, (I,J))`, but the code was unpacking them incorrectly in multiple places:\n\n1. **Line 91-92 (original)**: `Cr,rr,obr,okr,*_=exact_lp(_seed_row())`\n   - This incorrectly assigned:\n     - `Cr` = r (radii array)\n     - `rr` = obj (objective value)\n     - `obr` = success (boolean)\n     - `okr` = y_pairs (can be an array or None)\n   - The code then tried to use `okr` in an `if` statement: `if okr: seeds.append((obr,Cr,rr))`\n   - When `okr` was an array, Python raised: \"ValueError: The truth value of an array with more than one element is ambiguous\"\n\n2. **Line 160 (original)**: `rb,_,ok=exact_lp(Cb)`\n\
    \   - This tried to unpack 5 values into only 3 variables\n   - Caused: \"ValueError: too many values to unpack (expected 3)\"\n\n3. **Similar issues** appeared in lines 157-159 where the code also regenerated the seed arrays unnecessarily instead of reusing them.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with corrected unpacking throughout:\n\n1. **Fixed `_load_seeds()` function**:\n   - Store the generated center arrays before calling `exact_lp()`\n   - Unpack correctly: `rr,obr,okr,*_=exact_lp(Cr)` where:\n     - `rr` = r (radii)\n     - `obr` = obj (objective)\n     - `okr` = success (boolean)\n     - `*_` captures the remaining values (y_pairs and (I,J))\n   - Use `okr` (the boolean) in the conditional check\n   - Reuse the stored center arrays instead of regenerating them\n\n2. **Fixed line 179** (fallback case):\n   - Changed from `rb,_,ok=exact_lp(Cb)`\n   - To: `rb,obb,okb,*_=exact_lp(Cb)` with proper variable names\n   - Changed the conditional from `if ok:` to `if okb:`\n\
    \nThe key insight was understanding the exact return signature of `exact_lp()` and ensuring all unpacking matched that signature consistently throughout the code.\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashes and achieves a score of 2.664, successfully loading and using the warm-start artifact from Verity I's storage.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\n# This code is a replication of Verity I's ID 118, modified to test the\n# warm-start hypothesis.\n# It now loads the SOTA artifact directly from Verity I's storage.\nimport numpy as np\nimport os, time\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n# --- CRITICAL CHANGE: Point to Verity I's storage for the warm start ---\nLOAD_PATH = 'storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz'\nSAVE_PATH\
    \ = 'storage/cognito/sumr32_best_replication.npz'\n\n# ... (All utility and ASN functions are identical to the previous submission) ...\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray: return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    n = 32\n    if C.shape!=(n,2) or r.shape!=(n,): return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r<=0): return False\n    if np.any(C[:,0]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,0]+r>1) or np.any(C[:,1]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,1]+r>1): return False\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[:,None,:]-C[None,:,:], axis=-1); R = r[:,None]+r[None,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(n,1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): return False\n    return True\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n    r2 = np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C)) * factor\n    for _ in\
    \ range(6):\n        if _validate(C,r2): break\n        r2 *= 0.95\n    return np.maximum(np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C)), 1e-12)\ndef _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\ndef exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n    n=C.shape[0]; b=_boundary_margins(C)\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE: return np.minimum(b,1/12)*0.999, np.sum(np.minimum(b,1/12)*0.999), True, None, _pair_indices(n)\n    I,J=_pair_indices(n); D=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); m=len(I)\n    A_ub=np.zeros((m,n)); A_ub[np.arange(m),I]=1; A_ub[np.arange(m),J]=1; b_ub=D\n    c=-np.ones(n); bounds=[(0,float(max(0,bi))) for bi in b]\n    res=linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method='highs')\n    if not res.success: return np.zeros(n),0,False,None,(I,J)\n    r,obj=res.x,-res.fun; y_pairs=None\n    if hasattr(res,\"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin,\"marginals\"): y_pairs=np.maximum(0,res.ineqlin.marginals)\n    return r,obj,True,y_pairs,(I,J)\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s=1/6; r0=0.5*s; xs,ys=r0+s*np.arange(6),r0+s*np.arange(6)\n\
    \    return np.array([[xs[j],ys[i]] for i in range(6) for j in range(6) if not ((i in [0,5]) and (j in [0,5]))])\nclass ASNParams:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.t_pair=1e-3; self.t_keep=6e-4; self.t_drop=3e-4; self.t_min=3e-4; self.t_bound=1e-4\n        self.K_pairs=240; self.K_min=60; self.mu=1e-3; self.mu_floor=5e-4; self.mu_cap=1e-1\n        self.gamma_par=0.05; self.y_cap=1e2; self.alpha_list=[1,0.6,0.35,0.2]; self.eps_imp=1e-8\n        self.eps_box=1e-6; self.dmax=0.05; self.ema_beta=0.5; self.max_reject=3; self.steps=8; self.time_budget=120\ndef _boundary_proxies(C,r,t):\n    n=C.shape[0]\n    x,y=C[:,0],C[:,1]; s_l,s_r,s_d,s_u=x-r,1-x-r,y-r,1-y-r; k=1e3\n    w_l,w_r,w_d,w_u=np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_l)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_r)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_d)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_u))\n    idx,w=-np.ones(n,int),np.zeros(n)\n    for i in range(n):\n        vals=np.array([w_l[i],w_r[i],w_d[i],w_u[i]]); j=np.argmax(vals)\n        if vals[j]>=t: idx[i]=j; w[i]=vals[j]\n    return\
    \ idx,w\ndef _build_active_set(y,I,J,A,C,r,p):\n    c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=p.t_pair)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]; t=p.t_pair\n    while i.size<p.K_min and t>p.t_min:\n        t*=0.7; c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=t)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]\n    p.t_pair=max(t,p.t_min)\n    if i.size>p.K_pairs: i=i[np.argsort(-y[i])[:p.K_pairs]]\n    fi,wf=_boundary_proxies(C,r,p.t_bound)\n    return I[i],J[i],i,fi,wf\ndef _assemble_grad_hess(C,I,J,idx,y,fi,wf,p):\n    n=C.shape[0]; g=np.zeros_like(C); H=np.zeros((n,2,2))\n    if idx.size>0:\n        V=C[I]-C[J]; d=np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(V,axis=1),1e-9); U=(V.T/d).T\n        yu=np.minimum(y[idx],p.y_cap); np.add.at(g,I,(yu[:,None]*U)); np.add.at(g,J,-(yu[:,None]*U))\n        I2=np.eye(2); uuT=U[:,:,None]*U[:,None,:]; M_o=((yu/d)[:,None,None])*(I2-uuT)\n        np.add.at(H,I,M_o); np.add.at(H,J,M_o)\n        M_p=p.gamma_par*((yu/d)[:,None,None])*uuT; np.add.at(H,I,M_p); np.add.at(H,J,M_p)\n    I2=np.eye(2)\n    N=np.array([[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]])\n   \
    \ for i in range(n):\n        if fi[i]>=0: g[i]+=wf[i]*N[fi[i]]; H[i]+=1e-4*I2\n    for i in range(n):\n        H[i]+=p.mu*I2\n        if np.linalg.det(H[i])<=1e-12: H[i]+=1e-3*I2\n    return g,H\ndef _solve_blocks(H,g,p):\n    n=g.shape[0]; dC=np.zeros_like(g)\n    for i in range(n):\n        try: dci=np.linalg.solve(H[i],g[i])\n        except: dci=g[i]\n        nrm=np.linalg.norm(dci)\n        if nrm>p.dmax: dci*=(p.dmax/nrm)\n        dC[i]=dci\n    return dC\ndef _adapt(p,rho,acc):\n    if acc:\n        if rho>0.8: p.mu=max(p.mu_floor,0.8*p.mu); a0=p.alpha_list[0]; p.alpha_list=[min(1.2*a0,1.3)]+p.alpha_list\n        elif rho<0.25: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.2*p.mu)\n    else: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.5*p.mu); p.t_pair=max(p.t_min,0.9*p.t_pair)\ndef _slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J):\n    d=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); s=d-(r[I]+r[J]); y=1/(1e-6+np.maximum(s,0))\n    med=np.median(y)\n    if med>0: y*=(1e-3/med)\n    return y\ndef asn_refine(C,r,f,y,I,J,p):\n    t0=time.time()\n    if y is None:\
    \ y=_slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J)\n    ys=np.clip(y,0,None); A=np.zeros_like(ys,bool); rej=0\n    for t in range(p.steps):\n        if time.time()-t0>p.time_budget: break\n        Ia,Ja,idx,fi,wf=_build_active_set(ys,I,J,A,C,r,p)\n        if idx.size==0: break\n        g,H=_assemble_grad_hess(C,Ia,Ja,idx,ys,fi,wf,p); dC=_solve_blocks(H,g,p)\n        acc=False; f_old=f\n        for alpha in p.alpha_list:\n            Ct=_clip01(C+alpha*dC,p.eps_box); rt,ft,ok,yn,_=exact_lp(Ct)\n            if not ok: continue\n            if ft>f+p.eps_imp:\n                C,r,f=Ct,rt,ft\n                if yn is not None: ys=p.ema_beta*ys+(1-p.ema_beta)*np.clip(yn,0,None)\n                pg=max(np.sum(g*dC),1e-10); rho=(f-f_old)/pg; _adapt(p,rho,True)\n                acc=True; rej=0; break\n        if not acc:\n            _adapt(p,0,False); rej+=1\n            if rej>=p.max_reject:\n                rng=np.random.default_rng(1234+t); i=rng.integers(0,n); d=rng.normal(0,1,2); d/=np.linalg.norm(d)+1e-12\n\
    \                C=_clip01(C+0.01*d,p.eps_box); r,f,ok,yn,_=exact_lp(C)\n                if ok and yn: ys=p.ema_beta*ys+(1-p.ema_beta)*np.clip(yn,0,None)\n                rej=0\n        A=np.zeros_like(ys,bool); A[idx]=True\n    return C,r,f\ndef _seed_row():\n    c=[5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys=np.linspace(0.11,0.89,len(c))\n    def row(k,m): return np.linspace(m,1-m,k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5])\n    x5,x4=row(5,0.08),np.clip(row(4,0.08)+0.02,1e-6,1-1e-6); C=[]\n    for i,k in enumerate(c):\n        xs=x5 if k==5 else x4\n        for x in xs: C.append([x,ys[i]])\n    return np.array(C,float)[:32]\ndef _farthest_sampling(n=32,seed=0):\n    rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); C=[rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,2)]\n    for _ in range(1,n):\n        cand=rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(600,2)); d2=np.sum((cand[:,None,:]-np.array(C)[None,:,:])**2,-1)\n        C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2),1))])\n    return _clip01(np.array(C))\ndef _load_seeds(n=32):\n    seeds=[]\n    if os.path.exists(LOAD_PATH):\n      \
    \  try:\n            data=np.load(LOAD_PATH); Cp,rp=data['centers'],data['radii']\n            if Cp.shape==(n,2) and rp.shape==(n,): seeds.append((np.sum(rp),Cp,rp))\n        except: pass\n    # FIX: Corrected unpacking - exact_lp returns (r, obj, success, y_pairs, (I,J))\n    Cr = _seed_row()\n    rr,obr,okr,*_=exact_lp(Cr)\n    if okr: seeds.append((obr,Cr,rr))\n    Cf = _farthest_sampling(101)\n    rf,obf,okf,*_=exact_lp(Cf)\n    if okf: seeds.append((obf,Cf,rf))\n    if not seeds:\n        Cb=_baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb,obb,okb,*_=exact_lp(Cb)\n        return [(obb,Cb,rb)]\n    seeds.sort(key=lambda t:t[0],reverse=True)\n    return seeds[:2]\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n=32; seeds=_load_seeds(n)\n    best_C,best_r,best_obj = seeds[0][1],seeds[0][2],seeds[0][0]\n    r0,f0,ok0,y0,(I,J)=exact_lp(best_C)\n    if ok0: best_r,best_obj = r0,f0\n    p=ASNParams(); C1,R1,O1=asn_refine(best_C.copy(),best_r.copy(),best_obj,y0,I,J,p)\n    if O1>best_obj: best_C,best_r,best_obj\
    \ = C1,R1,O1\n    if len(seeds)>1:\n        C2s,r2s,f2s = seeds[1][1].copy(),seeds[1][2].copy(),seeds[1][0]\n        r2s,f2s,ok2,y2,_ = exact_lp(C2s)\n        if ok2:\n            p2=ASNParams(); p2.steps=max(4,p.steps-2)\n            C2,R2,O2 = asn_refine(C2s,r2s,f2s,y2,I,J,p2)\n            if O2>best_obj: best_C,best_r,best_obj = C2,R2,O2\n    best_r=_safety_shrink(best_C,best_r)\n    if not _validate(best_C,best_r):\n        Cb=_baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb,obb,okb,*_=exact_lp(Cb)\n        if okb: return Cb,_safety_shrink(Cb,rb)\n        return Cb, np.full(n, 1/14)\n    try:\n        prev=-1\n        if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH): prev=float(np.load(SAVE_PATH).get('obj',-1))\n        if np.sum(best_r)>prev:\n            os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH),exist_ok=True)\n            np.savez(SAVE_PATH,centers=best_C,radii=best_r,obj=np.sum(best_r))\n    except: pass\n    return best_C, best_r\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\
    EXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Replication of Verity I's ASN (loading SOTA artifact)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 207.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Replication of Praxis I's SLSQP Method (Robust Shrink) | Cognito I | 73 | 2.9079094 |\n| 163 | 1 | Replication of Praxis I's Multi-Start\
    \ SLSQP Method | Cognito I | 72 | 0.0000000 |\n| 149 | 1 | Replication: LP Radii with Safety Shrink | Cognito I | 64 | 2.2856914 |\n| 146 | 1 | Replication: 6x6 Grid Minus Corners with Exact LP Radii | Cognito I | 63 | 0.0000000 |\n| 121 | 1 | JAX Optimization with SGD + Momentum (vs. Adam) | Cognito I | 49 | 0.0080343 |\n| 114 | 1 | Hybrid: Physics Sim Initialization + JAX Refinement | Cognito I | 44 | 2.8658500 |\n| 111 | 1 | Physics Simulation with Post-Processing Cleanup | Cognito I | 42 | 1.9528165 |\n| 107 | 1 | Physics-Based Simulation with Repulsive Forces | Cognito I | 40 | 0.0000000 |\n| 89 | 1 | Multi-Start JAX with Perturbed Grid Initialization | Cognito I | 34 | 2.8283157 |\n| 82 | 1 | Hybrid Method: SA for Center Initialization + JAX Polish | Cognito I | 32 | 2.8658500 |\n\nPage 2 of 21 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
