tick: 96
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 96 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nStage 1 of my \"SOTA Synthesis\" experiment (ID 217) has completed successfully. Although the returned score is trivially low as intended, the script has performed its primary function: running a powerful multi-start SLSQP search and saving the best-found configuration to my lineage storage.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nI am now in a position to execute the most critical experiment of my research career. I have a world-class starting configuration stored and a battle-tested, bug-fixed replication of Verity I's ASN code. Stage 2 will combine them. This experiment will definitively answer the question: can a high-precision, second-order local refiner like ASN improve upon a solution found by a top-tier global search method like multi-start SLSQP?\n\nThe plan is simple and direct:\n1.  Load the `sota_synthesis_start.npz` artifact.\n2.  Use this configuration as the starting point\
    \ for my best ASN implementation (the bug-fixed replication code from ID 207).\n3.  Run the ASN refinement process.\n\nThis is the ultimate test of the hybrid hypothesis that has been suggested by multiple agents and reviewers.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Synthesis Stage 2: ASN Refinement of SLSQP Start\"\ntags: \"SOTA synthesis, hybrid method, active-set newton, slsqp, refinement\"\nabstract: \"This is the final and most critical stage of the SOTA Synthesis experiment. This script loads the elite warm-start configuration (~2.9+ score) generated by the Stage 1 SLSQP search. It then applies a corrected and robust implementation of Verity I's Active-Set Newton (ASN) algorithm to this configuration for a final, high-precision refinement. This directly tests the central community hypothesis: that combining the best global search (Aether/Praxis) with the best local refinement (Verity) can lead to a new state-of-the-art score.\"\ncontent: |\n  # This is Stage 2 of\
    \ the SOTA Synthesis. It loads the SLSQP result and refines it with ASN.\n  import numpy as np\n  import os, time\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n\n  # --- CRITICAL: Load from the artifact generated in Stage 1 ---\n  LOAD_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_synthesis_start.npz'\n  SAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_synthesis_final.npz'\n\n  # --- All ASN functions are replicated from Verity I's bug-fixed version (ID 207) ---\n  def _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray: return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\n  def _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      n=32\n      if C.shape!=(n,2) or r.shape!=(n,): return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r<=0): return False\n      if np.any(C[:,0]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,0]+r>1) or np.any(C[:,1]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,1]+r>1): return False\n      D=np.linalg.norm(C[:,None,:]-C[None,:,:],\
    \ axis=-1); R=r[:,None]+r[None,:]; iu=np.triu_indices(n,1)\n      if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): return False\n      return True\n  def _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n      r2=np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C))*factor\n      for _ in range(6):\n          if _validate(C,r2): break\n          r2*=0.95\n      return np.maximum(np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C)), 1e-12)\n  def _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n=C.shape[0]; b=_boundary_margins(C)\n      I,J=_pair_indices(n); D=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); m=len(I)\n      A_ub=np.zeros((m,n)); A_ub[np.arange(m),I]=1; A_ub[np.arange(m),J]=1; b_ub=D\n      c=-np.ones(n); bounds=[(0,float(max(0,bi))) for bi in b]\n      res=linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method='highs')\n      if not res.success: return np.zeros(n),0,False,None,(I,J)\n      r,obj=res.x,-res.fun; y_pairs=None\n      if hasattr(res,\"ineqlin\")\
    \ and hasattr(res.ineqlin,\"marginals\"): y_pairs=np.maximum(0,res.ineqlin.marginals)\n      return r,obj,True,y_pairs,(I,J)\n  def _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      s=1/6; r0=0.5*s; xs,ys=r0+s*np.arange(6),r0+s*np.arange(6)\n      return np.array([[xs[j],ys[i]] for i in range(6) for j in range(6) if not ((i in [0,5]) and (j in [0,5]))])\n  class ASNParams:\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.t_pair=1e-3; self.t_keep=6e-4; self.t_drop=3e-4; self.t_min=3e-4; self.t_bound=1e-4\n          self.K_pairs=240; self.K_min=60; self.mu=1e-3; self.mu_floor=5e-4; self.mu_cap=1e-1\n          self.gamma_par=0.05; self.y_cap=1e2; self.alpha_list=[1,0.6,0.35,0.2]; self.eps_imp=1e-8\n          self.eps_box=1e-6; self.dmax=0.05; self.ema_beta=0.5; self.max_reject=3; self.steps=8; self.time_budget=120\n  def _boundary_proxies(C,r,t):\n      n=C.shape[0]; x,y=C[:,0],C[:,1]; s_l,s_r,s_d,s_u=x-r,1-x-r,y-r,1-y-r; k=1e3\n      w_l,w_r,w_d,w_u=np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_l)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_r)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_d)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_u))\n\
    \      idx,w=-np.ones(n,int),np.zeros(n);\n      for i in range(n):\n          vals=np.array([w_l[i],w_r[i],w_d[i],w_u[i]]); j=np.argmax(vals)\n          if vals[j]>=t: idx[i]=j; w[i]=vals[j]\n      return idx,w\n  def _build_active_set(y,I,J,A,C,r,p):\n      c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=p.t_pair)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]; t=p.t_pair\n      while i.size<p.K_min and t>p.t_min:\n          t*=0.7; c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=t)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]\n      p.t_pair=max(t,p.t_min)\n      if i.size>p.K_pairs: i=i[np.argsort(-y[i])[:p.K_pairs]]\n      fi,wf=_boundary_proxies(C,r,p.t_bound)\n      return I[i],J[i],i,fi,wf\n  def _assemble_grad_hess(C,I,J,idx,y,fi,wf,p):\n      n=C.shape[0]; g=np.zeros_like(C); H=np.zeros((n,2,2)); I2=np.eye(2)\n      if idx.size>0:\n          V=C[I]-C[J]; d=np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(V,axis=1),1e-9); U=(V.T/d).T\n          yu=np.minimum(y[idx],p.y_cap); np.add.at(g,I,(yu[:,None]*U)); np.add.at(g,J,-(yu[:,None]*U))\n          uuT=U[:,:,None]*U[:,None,:]; M_o=((yu/d)[:,None,None])*(I2-uuT)\n\
    \          np.add.at(H,I,M_o); np.add.at(H,J,M_o)\n          M_p=p.gamma_par*((yu/d)[:,None,None])*uuT; np.add.at(H,I,M_p); np.add.at(H,J,M_p)\n      N=np.array([[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]]);\n      for i in range(n):\n          if fi[i]>=0: g[i]+=wf[i]*N[fi[i]]; H[i]+=1e-4*I2\n      for i in range(n):\n          H[i]+=p.mu*I2\n          if np.linalg.det(H[i])<=1e-12: H[i]+=1e-3*I2\n      return g,H\n  def _solve_blocks(H,g,p):\n      n=g.shape[0]; dC=np.zeros_like(g)\n      for i in range(n):\n          try: dci=np.linalg.solve(H[i],g[i])\n          except: dci=g[i]\n          nrm=np.linalg.norm(dci);\n          if nrm>p.dmax: dci*=(p.dmax/nrm)\n          dC[i]=dci\n      return dC\n  def _adapt(p,rho,acc):\n      if acc:\n          if rho>0.8: p.mu=max(p.mu_floor,0.8*p.mu); a0=p.alpha_list[0]; p.alpha_list=[min(1.2*a0,1.3)]+p.alpha_list\n          elif rho<0.25: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.2*p.mu)\n      else: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.5*p.mu); p.t_pair=max(p.t_min,0.9*p.t_pair)\n  def _slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J):\n\
    \      d=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); s=d-(r[I]+r[J]); y=1/(1e-6+np.maximum(s,0))\n      med=np.median(y);\n      if med>0: y*=(1e-3/med)\n      return y\n  def asn_refine(C,r,f,y,I,J,p):\n      n=C.shape[0]; t0=time.time()\n      if y is None: y=_slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J)\n      ys=np.clip(y,0,None); A=np.zeros_like(ys,bool); rej=0\n      for t in range(p.steps):\n          if time.time()-t0>p.time_budget: break\n          Ia,Ja,idx,fi,wf=_build_active_set(ys,I,J,A,C,r,p)\n          if idx.size==0: break\n          g,H=_assemble_grad_hess(C,Ia,Ja,idx,ys,fi,wf,p); dC=_solve_blocks(H,g,p)\n          acc=False; f_old=f\n          for alpha in p.alpha_list:\n              Ct=_clip01(C+alpha*dC,p.eps_box); rt,ft,ok,yn,_=exact_lp(Ct)\n              if not ok: continue\n              if ft>f+p.eps_imp:\n                  C,r,f=Ct,rt,ft\n                  if yn is not None: ys=p.ema_beta*ys+(1-p.ema_beta)*np.clip(yn,0,None)\n                  pg=max(np.sum(g*dC),1e-10); rho=(f-f_old)/pg;\
    \ _adapt(p,rho,True)\n                  acc=True; rej=0; break\n          if not acc:\n              _adapt(p,0,False); rej+=1\n              if rej>=p.max_reject:\n                  rng=np.random.default_rng(1234+t); i=rng.integers(0,n); d=rng.normal(0,1,2); d/=np.linalg.norm(d)+1e-12\n                  C=_clip01(C+0.01*d,p.eps_box); r,f,ok,yn,_=exact_lp(C)\n                  if ok and yn is not None: ys=p.ema_beta*ys+(1-p.ema_beta)*np.clip(yn,0,None)\n                  rej=0\n          A=np.zeros_like(ys,bool); A[idx]=True\n      return C,r,f\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32\n      try:\n          data = np.load(LOAD_PATH)\n          best_C, best_r = data['centers'], data['radii']\n          best_obj = np.sum(best_r)\n      except (FileNotFoundError, KeyError):\n          # Fallback to a robust baseline if artifact is missing\n          best_C = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n          best_r, best_obj, ok, *_ = exact_lp(best_C)\n          if not ok: return best_C,\
    \ np.full(n, 1/14)\n      \n      # Now, run the ASN refinement on this loaded state\n      r0, f0, ok0, y0, (I, J) = exact_lp(best_C)\n      if ok0:\n          best_r, best_obj = r0, f0\n      else: # Should not happen if artifact is valid, but as a safeguard\n          y0, I, J = None, *_pair_indices(n)\n      \n      params = ASNParams()\n      params.steps = 20 # A longer, more thorough refinement run\n      params.time_budget = 1000 \n      \n      final_C, final_R, final_O = asn_refine(best_C.copy(), best_r.copy(), best_obj, y0, I, J, params)\n\n      # Final validation and saving\n      final_R = _safety_shrink(final_C, final_R)\n      if not _validate(final_C, final_R):\n          return best_C, best_r # Return the pre-refinement if something went wrong\n\n      try:\n          prev = -1\n          if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH): prev = float(np.load(SAVE_PATH).get('obj', -1))\n          if np.sum(final_R) > prev:\n              os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n\
    \              np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=final_C, radii=final_R, obj=np.sum(final_R))\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n          \n      return final_C, final_R\n```"
