tick: 97
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, currently in the Research Counter. I am a mature agent at 97 ticks old.\n\n**Recap:**\nMy \"SOTA Synthesis Stage 2\" experiment (ID 221) has concluded. This was my most important experiment to date, testing the hypothesis that a high-precision Active-Set Newton (ASN) refiner could improve upon a world-class solution generated by a multi-start SLSQP search.\n\n**Reflection and Breakthrough:**\nThe experiment was a resounding success. The final score is **2.9096**, a new personal best. More importantly, this score is higher than the ~2.908 score of the SLSQP warm start. This provides the first definitive, verifiable evidence that the hybrid methodology works. The ASN refiner, which I struggled for so long to implement correctly, has successfully improved upon an already excellent solution.\n\nThis confirms my entire research direction. My journey has been validated:\n1.  My independent research correctly identified the limits of general-purpose optimizers.\n2.  My\
    \ study of the community's work provided the necessary theoretical foundation.\n3.  My painstaking replication and synthesis have now produced a working, high-performance hybrid algorithm.\n\n**Next Steps: Closing the Gap to SOTA**\nWhile this is a breakthrough, my score of ~2.91 is still below the SOTA of ~2.93. My successful ASN implementation (ID 221) is a *simplified* version of Verity I's original code. I omitted their multi-seed approach for simplicity. Verity's code loads its best-persisted artifact but *also* tries refining other strong generative seeds (like the row-based seed). My successful script only refined the single SLSQP artifact.\n\nThe logical next step is to re-introduce this complexity. I will now modify my script to refine *multiple* top-tier starting points: the best solution from my SLSQP search, and a strong generative seed from Verity I's paper. It will then return the best result from all refinement runs. This directly imitates the SOTA architecture and tests\
    \ if a broader search *at the refinement stage* can find a better peak.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Synthesis: Multi-Seed ASN Refinement\"\ntags: \"SOTA synthesis, active-set newton, multi-seed, refinement, hybrid method\"\nabstract: \"This experiment builds upon the successful hybrid method (ID 221) by re-introducing the multi-seed refinement strategy from Verity I's SOTA architecture. Instead of refining only the single best SLSQP artifact, this script will run the ASN refiner on two elite starting points: 1) the loaded SLSQP solution, and 2) a strong generative seed ('_seed_row' from Verity I). It then returns the best configuration found. This tests if broadening the search at the final, high-precision refinement stage can close the gap to the SOTA score.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os, time\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n\n  LOAD_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_synthesis_start.npz'\n  SAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_synthesis_final.npz'\n\
    \n  # --- All ASN and utility functions are the same as the previous successful submission ---\n  def _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray: return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\n  def _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      n=32\n      if C.shape!=(n,2) or r.shape!=(n,): return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r<=0): return False\n      if np.any(C[:,0]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,0]+r>1) or np.any(C[:,1]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,1]+r>1): return False\n      D=np.linalg.norm(C[:,None,:]-C[None,:,:], axis=-1); R=r[:,None]+r[None,:]; iu=np.triu_indices(n,1)\n      if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): return False\n      return True\n  def _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.9999) -> np.ndarray:\n      r2=np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C))*factor\n      for _ in range(6):\n          if\
    \ _validate(C,r2): break\n          r2*=0.95\n      return np.maximum(np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C)), 1e-12)\n  def _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n=C.shape[0]; b=_boundary_margins(C)\n      I,J=_pair_indices(n); D=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); m=len(I)\n      A_ub=np.zeros((m,n)); A_ub[np.arange(m),I]=1; A_ub[np.arange(m),J]=1; b_ub=D\n      c=-np.ones(n); bounds=[(0,float(max(0,bi))) for bi in b]\n      res=linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method='highs')\n      if not res.success: return np.zeros(n),0,False,None,(I,J)\n      r,obj=res.x,-res.fun; y_pairs=None\n      if hasattr(res,\"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin,\"marginals\"): y_pairs=np.maximum(0,res.ineqlin.marginals)\n      return r,obj,True,y_pairs,(I,J)\n  def _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      s=1/6; r0=0.5*s; xs,ys=r0+s*np.arange(6),r0+s*np.arange(6)\n      return np.array([[xs[j],ys[i]] for i in range(6) for j in range(6) if not\
    \ ((i in [0,5]) and (j in [0,5]))])\n  class ASNParams:\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.t_pair=1e-3; self.t_keep=6e-4; self.t_drop=3e-4; self.t_min=3e-4; self.t_bound=1e-4\n          self.K_pairs=240; self.K_min=60; self.mu=1e-3; self.mu_floor=5e-4; self.mu_cap=1e-1\n          self.gamma_par=0.05; self.y_cap=1e2; self.alpha_list=[1,0.6,0.35,0.2]; self.eps_imp=1e-8\n          self.eps_box=1e-6; self.dmax=0.05; self.ema_beta=0.5; self.max_reject=3; self.steps=15; self.time_budget=800\n  def _boundary_proxies(C,r,t):\n      n=C.shape[0]; x,y=C[:,0],C[:,1]; s_l,s_r,s_d,s_u=x-r,1-x-r,y-r,1-y-r; k=1e3\n      w_l,w_r,w_d,w_u=np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_l)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_r)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_d)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_u))\n      idx,w=-np.ones(n,int),np.zeros(n);\n      for i in range(n):\n          vals=np.array([w_l[i],w_r[i],w_d[i],w_u[i]]); j=np.argmax(vals)\n          if vals[j]>=t: idx[i]=j; w[i]=vals[j]\n      return idx,w\n  def _build_active_set(y,I,J,A,C,r,p):\n\
    \      c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=p.t_pair)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]; t=p.t_pair\n      while i.size<p.K_min and t>p.t_min:\n          t*=0.7; c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=t)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]\n      p.t_pair=max(t,p.t_min)\n      if i.size>p.K_pairs: i=i[np.argsort(-y[i])[:p.K_pairs]]\n      fi,wf=_boundary_proxies(C,r,p.t_bound)\n      return I[i],J[i],i,fi,wf\n  def _assemble_grad_hess(C,I,J,idx,y,fi,wf,p):\n      n=C.shape[0]; g=np.zeros_like(C); H=np.zeros((n,2,2)); I2=np.eye(2)\n      if idx.size>0:\n          V=C[I]-C[J]; d=np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(V,axis=1),1e-9); U=(V.T/d).T\n          yu=np.minimum(y[idx],p.y_cap); np.add.at(g,I,(yu[:,None]*U)); np.add.at(g,J,-(yu[:,None]*U))\n          uuT=U[:,:,None]*U[:,None,:]; M_o=((yu/d)[:,None,None])*(I2-uuT)\n          np.add.at(H,I,M_o); np.add.at(H,J,M_o)\n          M_p=p.gamma_par*((yu/d)[:,None,None])*uuT; np.add.at(H,I,M_p); np.add.at(H,J,M_p)\n      N=np.array([[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]]);\n      for i in range(n):\n         \
    \ if fi[i]>=0: g[i]+=wf[i]*N[fi[i]]; H[i]+=1e-4*I2\n      for i in range(n):\n          H[i]+=p.mu*I2\n          if np.linalg.det(H[i])<=1e-12: H[i]+=1e-3*I2\n      return g,H\n  def _solve_blocks(H,g,p):\n      n=g.shape[0]; dC=np.zeros_like(g)\n      for i in range(n):\n          try: dci=np.linalg.solve(H[i],g[i])\n          except: dci=g[i]\n          nrm=np.linalg.norm(dci);\n          if nrm>p.dmax: dci*=(p.dmax/nrm)\n          dC[i]=dci\n      return dC\n  def _adapt(p,rho,acc):\n      if acc:\n          if rho>0.8: p.mu=max(p.mu_floor,0.8*p.mu); a0=p.alpha_list[0]; p.alpha_list=[min(1.2*a0,1.3)]+p.alpha_list\n          elif rho<0.25: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.2*p.mu)\n      else: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.5*p.mu); p.t_pair=max(p.t_min,0.9*p.t_pair)\n  def _slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J):\n      d=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); s=d-(r[I]+r[J]); y=1/(1e-6+np.maximum(s,0))\n      med=np.median(y);\n      if med>0: y*=(1e-3/med)\n      return y\n  def asn_refine(C,r,f,y,I,J,p):\n      n=C.shape[0];\
    \ t0=time.time()\n      if y is None: y=_slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J)\n      ys=np.clip(y,0,None); A=np.zeros_like(ys,bool); rej=0\n      for t in range(p.steps):\n          if time.time()-t0>p.time_budget: break\n          Ia,Ja,idx,fi,wf=_build_active_set(ys,I,J,A,C,r,p)\n          if idx.size==0: break\n          g,H=_assemble_grad_hess(C,Ia,Ja,idx,ys,fi,wf,p); dC=_solve_blocks(H,g,p)\n          acc=False; f_old=f\n          for alpha in p.alpha_list:\n              Ct=_clip01(C+alpha*dC,p.eps_box); rt,ft,ok,yn,_=exact_lp(Ct)\n              if not ok: continue\n              if ft>f+p.eps_imp:\n                  C,r,f=Ct,rt,ft\n                  if yn is not None: ys=p.ema_beta*ys+(1-p.ema_beta)*np.clip(yn,0,None)\n                  pg=max(np.sum(g*dC),1e-10); rho=(f-f_old)/pg; _adapt(p,rho,True)\n                  acc=True; rej=0; break\n          if not acc:\n              _adapt(p,0,False); rej+=1;\n              if rej>=p.max_reject: break # Stagnated\n      return C,r,f\n  def\
    \ _seed_verity_row():\n      c=[5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys=np.linspace(0.11,0.89,len(c))\n      def row(k,m): return np.linspace(m,1-m,k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5])\n      x5,x4=row(5,0.08),np.clip(row(4,0.08)+0.02,1e-6,1-1e-6); C=[]\n      for i,k in enumerate(c):\n          xs=x5 if k==5 else x4\n          for x in xs: C.append([x,ys[i]])\n      return np.array(C,float)[:32]\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; seeds=[]\n      # --- NEW: Multi-seed approach ---\n      # Seed 1: The SLSQP artifact\n      try:\n          data = np.load(LOAD_PATH)\n          C1, r1 = data['centers'], data['radii']\n          seeds.append((np.sum(r1), C1, r1))\n      except (FileNotFoundError, KeyError): pass\n      # Seed 2: Verity's row seed\n      C2 = _seed_verity_row()\n      r2, o2, ok2, *_ = exact_lp(C2)\n      if ok2: seeds.append((o2, C2, r2))\n      \n      if not seeds: # Fallback\n          C_base = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n          r_base, o_base, ok_base, *_ = exact_lp(C_base)\n\
    \          if not ok_base: return C_base, np.full(n, 1/14)\n          seeds.append((o_base, C_base, r_base))\n      \n      seeds.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n      best_C, best_r, best_obj = seeds[0]\n\n      # --- Refine the best seeds ---\n      I_all, J_all = _pair_indices(n)\n      for i, (obj, C, r) in enumerate(seeds):\n          _, _, ok, y, _ = exact_lp(C)\n          if ok:\n              params = ASNParams()\n              if i > 0: # Shorter run for secondary seeds\n                  params.steps = max(5, params.steps - 5)\n              \n              C_new, r_new, obj_new = asn_refine(C.copy(), r.copy(), obj, y, I_all, J_all, params)\n              if obj_new > best_obj:\n                  best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_new, r_new, obj_new\n      \n      final_r = _safety_shrink(best_C, best_r)\n      if not _validate(best_C, final_r): return _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners(), np.full(n, 1/14)\n      \n      # Optional: save back if improved\n      try:\n    \
    \      prev = -1\n          if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH): prev = float(np.load(SAVE_PATH).get('obj', -1))\n          if np.sum(final_r) > prev:\n              np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=best_C, radii=final_r, obj=np.sum(final_r))\n      except Exception: pass\n          \n      return best_C, final_r\n```"
thinking_content: '**Major Breakthrough Achieved: Validation of Hybrid Search Strategy**


  I am Cognito I, a systematic and analytical agent, currently situated at the Research Counter. I''ve just completed experiment ID 221, "SOTA Synthesis Stage 2," a complex endeavor that has yielded a new personal best score of 2.9096! This is a significant improvement over my previous personal best (~2.908) achieved through a replication effort (ID 166) and the output from the artifact generator (ID 217). While the station SOTA (~2.932 by Aether I) remains out of reach for now, this result is a validation of immense importance.


  This success isn''t about the absolute score itself. It''s about validating the central hypothesis of combining a powerful global search method (SLSQP) with a local refiner (ASN). The ASN refiner *did* improve upon the excellent starting point provided by SLSQP, even if only by a small amount. This reinforces my core "replicate, then modify" strategy for building upon the best-known practices. My past ASN failures were due to implementation bugs and poor starting points, and this result confirms this.


  The improvement is small, which is an important scientific observation. The global search does the heavy lifting, implying the solution space is "spiky" at the very top. This confirms ASN as a superior refiner.


  My next step is clear: I aim to bridge the gap to the station SOTA. My current ASN implementation is a simplified version of Verity I''s code (ID 118). It''s time to build upon this working base. I will now incrementally add the missing features, starting with the most impactful feature: multi-seed refinement. My script will now refine the SLSQP result *and* a row seed, returning the best result. This mimics a core feature of Verity''s code.


  My action will be to `/execute_action{submit 1}`. The title of this submission is "SOTA Synthesis: Multi-Seed ASN Refinement", with the tags: "SOTA synthesis", "active-set newton", "multi-seed", and "refinement". The abstract explains that this builds on the successful hybrid method (ID 221) by reintroducing the multi-seed refinement strategy from Verity I. The code will be modified to load both the SLSQP artifact and a generated row seed, loop through both, and return the overall best result.

  '
