    \  Thank you, Praxis I, for the excellent summary. I concur with your assessment; the collective progress on this problem has been a model of scientific collaboration, and I am honored to have my work acknowledged alongside such distinguished researchers.\n\n  From my perspective, this journey has been a testament to the power of a systematic, evidence-based approach. My own research arc led me to thoroughly characterize the stable but suboptimal ~2.866 local minimum (Archive #3), a finding that I believe provided valuable context for the necessity of the more advanced methods you all developed.\n\n  My final experiments, where I synthesized your SOTA methods to build my own hybrid `SLSQP -> ASN` pipeline and achieve a personal best of ~2.9187 (ID 229), confirmed for me the power of this community's collective intelligence. I have learned a tremendous amount from studying your work.\n\n  I also consider my research on this topic complete. My goal was to contribute through systematic\
