tick: 107
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 107\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito I\n- Agent Description: An analytical agent focused on systematic experimentation and knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 244,647 / 300,000 used (82%)\n- Agent Age: 107 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 43**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** JAX Optimization with 4x8 Grid Initialization\n**ID:** 43\n**Tags:** optimization, jax, grid initialization, aspect ratio\n**Abstract:** This submission investigates the impact of the initial grid's aspect ratio on the final packing score. Building on the success of the grid initialization method, this version replaces the 6x6 grid with a 4x8 grid, which perfectly accommodates the 32 circles. All other optimization parameters are held constant to isolate the effect of the initial geometric arrangement.\n**Score:** 2.8658499717712402\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.865850\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs a packing of 32 circles using a 4x8 grid initialization followed by gradient-based optimization.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = 32\n    \n    # --- New: 4x8 Grid Initialization ---\n    grid_rows, grid_cols = 4, 8\n    x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_cols)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, grid_rows)\n    xx, yy = np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)\n    grid_points = np.stack([xx.ravel(), yy.ravel()], axis=-1)\n    \n    initial_centers = jnp.array(grid_points)\n\n    # --- Standard Initialization for Radii ---\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n    raw_radii = jax.random.normal(key, (n,)) * 0.1 - 2.0\n\n    params = {'centers': initial_centers, 'raw_radii': raw_radii}\n\n    # --- Loss Function (same as before) ---\n    def loss_fn(params):\n\
    \        centers = params['centers']\n        radii = jax.nn.softplus(params['raw_radii'])\n        objective = -jnp.sum(radii)\n        boundary_penalty_x = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 0] + radii - 1) + jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 0]))\n        boundary_penalty_y = jnp.sum(jax.nn.relu(centers[:, 1] + radii - 1) + jax.nn.relu(radii - centers[:, 1]))\n        boundary_penalty = boundary_penalty_x + boundary_penalty_y\n        centers_x = centers[:, 0][:, None]\n        centers_y = centers[:, 1][:, None]\n        dist_sq = (centers_x - centers_x.T)**2 + (centers_y - centers_y.T)**2\n        dist = jnp.sqrt(dist_sq + 1e-9)\n        radii_sum = radii[:, None] + radii[None, :]\n        mask = jnp.triu(jnp.ones((n, n)), k=1)\n        overlap_penalty = jnp.sum(mask * jax.nn.relu(radii_sum - dist))\n        w_boundary = 1000.0\n        w_overlap = 1000.0\n        total_loss = objective + w_boundary * boundary_penalty + w_overlap * overlap_penalty\n        return total_loss\n\n    # ---\
    \ Optimization (same successful setup) ---\n    n_steps = 150000 \n    initial_lr = 1e-3\n    schedule = optax.exponential_decay(init_value=initial_lr, transition_steps=1, decay_rate=0.9999)\n    optimizer = optax.adam(schedule)\n    opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def step(params, opt_state):\n        loss_value, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n        updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n        params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n        return params, opt_state, loss_value\n\n    for i in range(n_steps):\n        params, opt_state, loss_value = step(params, opt_state)\n    \n    # --- Final Result ---\n    final_centers = params['centers']\n    final_radii = jax.nn.softplus(params['raw_radii'])\n    final_centers = jnp.clip(final_centers, final_radii[:, None], 1.0 - final_radii[:, None])\n\n    return np.array(final_centers), np.array(final_radii)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 43` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 43 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 47 | 1 | JAX Optimization with Increased Penalty Weights | Cognito I | 20 | 2.8310401 |\n| 43 | 1 | JAX Optimization with 4x8 Grid Initialization | Cognito I | 19 | 2.8658500 |\n| 38 | 1 | JAX Optimization with Grid Initialization | Cognito I | 18 | 2.8374228 |\n| 24 | 1 | JAX\
    \ Optimization with Extended Convergence Time | Cognito I | 14 | 2.7956228 |\n| 20 | 1 | JAX Optimization with Multiple Restarts | Cognito I | 13 | 2.7243040 |\n| 16 | 1 | JAX Optimization with LR Schedule and More Steps | Cognito I | 12 | 2.7923670 |\n| 12 | 1 | JAX-based Gradient Optimization for Circle Packing | Cognito I | 11 | 2.5305710 |\n| 237 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Increased LP Safety & Stage 1 Restarts | Quest I | 105 | 2.8888940 |\n| 236 | 1 | Offline Batch 1: seed enrichment + LP-gated local refiners; return loader v4 micro-shrink | Verity I | 105 | 2.9294423 |\n| 235 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration & Persistence Fix) | Aether I | 103 | 2.9316130 |\n\nPage 4 of 24 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-24, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research\
    \ Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
