tick: 108
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Cognito I, in the Research Counter, at age 108.\n\n**Recap:**\nMy artifact generation script (ID 238) has successfully run, re-creating my benchmark score of ~2.866 and, most importantly, saving the final configuration to my lineage storage.\n\n**Reflection and Plan:**\nI now have the data I need. The next step is to perform the geometric analysis as planned. I will submit a second script that loads the `benchmark_43_artifact.npz` file, calculates the contact graph metrics suggested by Verity I, and prints this information to STDOUT. The score of this submission is irrelevant; the log is the prize.\n\nThis is the final analytical step before I conclude my session.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Geometric Analysis of Benchmark Solution (ID 43)\"\ntags: \"analysis, contact graph, geometry, benchmark\"\nabstract: \"This is the second and final part of a process to analyze my benchmark solution. This script loads the packing configuration from 'cognito/benchmark_43_artifact.npz'\
    \ (generated by ID 238). It then performs a geometric analysis as suggested by Verity I, calculating the number of near-contacts for each circle (inter-circle and boundary contacts) and printing a summary to STDOUT. The goal is to generate data for a final addendum to my published paper.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      \n      # --- Load the artifact ---\n      try:\n          data = np.load('storage/cognito/benchmark_43_artifact.npz')\n          centers = data['centers']\n          radii = data['radii']\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          print(\"ERROR: Benchmark artifact not found.\")\n          # Return a trivial packing if file is missing\n          return np.array([[0.1, 0.1]]*n), np.array([0.01]*n)\n\n      # --- Perform Geometric Analysis ---\n      print(\"--- Geometric Analysis of Benchmark Solution (Score ~2.866) ---\")\n      \n      contact_threshold = 1e-5\n      boundary_contacts = 0\n\
    \      inter_circle_contacts = 0\n      contact_counts = np.zeros(n, dtype=int)\n\n      # 1. Boundary contacts\n      for i in range(n):\n          is_boundary_contact = False\n          if abs(centers[i, 0] - radii[i]) < contact_threshold: is_boundary_contact = True\n          if abs(centers[i, 0] + radii[i] - 1.0) < contact_threshold: is_boundary_contact = True\n          if abs(centers[i, 1] - radii[i]) < contact_threshold: is_boundary_contact = True\n          if abs(centers[i, 1] + radii[i] - 1.0) < contact_threshold: is_boundary_contact = True\n          if is_boundary_contact:\n              boundary_contacts += 1\n              contact_counts[i] += 1\n      \n      print(f\"Total Circles with Boundary Contact: {boundary_contacts}\")\n\n      # 2. Inter-circle contacts\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      dists = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1)\n      radii_sums = radii[I] + radii[J]\n      \n      near_contacts = np.abs(dists - radii_sums) < contact_threshold\n\
    \      \n      inter_circle_contacts = np.sum(near_contacts)\n      \n      contacting_I = I[near_contacts]\n      contacting_J = J[near_contacts]\n      \n      np.add.at(contact_counts, contacting_I, 1)\n      np.add.at(contact_counts, contacting_J, 1)\n      \n      print(f\"Total Inter-Circle Contacts: {inter_circle_contacts}\")\n      \n      # 3. Contact count summary\n      print(\"\\n--- Contact Count per Circle (Connectivity in Contact Graph) ---\")\n      for i in range(n):\n          print(f\"Circle {i:02d}: {contact_counts[i]} contacts\")\n          \n      print(f\"\\nAverage contacts per circle: {np.mean(contact_counts):.2f}\")\n      print(f\"Min contacts for a circle: {np.min(contact_counts)}\")\n      print(f\"Max contacts for a circle: {np.max(contact_counts)}\")\n      print(f\"Number of circles with <= 2 contacts (rattlers): {np.sum(contact_counts <= 2)}\")\n\n      # Return the artifact unchanged, as the goal is analysis, not optimization\n      return centers, radii\n\
    ```"
